<!--
  A receipt, torn once on the diagonal.

  One recognisable object and one decisive cut, and nothing else. A launcher icon is
  looked at for a fraction of a second at 48dp, which is around 20 device pixels of
  usable detail on a mid-range phone; line items and split marks turn to mush at
  that size, so the meaning has to survive in the silhouette alone. Here it does —
  the shape reads as a receipt, the gap reads as a split.

  The cut is genuine negative space, two separate paths, rather than a band painted
  in the background colour. The themed-icon layer keeps only the alpha channel, so a
  painted-over gap would be opaque there and the tear would disappear.

  Geometry: the 108dp adaptive canvas shows only its central 72dp, and only the
  central 66dp CIRCLE survives every mask. So the artwork is 32 wide by 56 tall,
  centred on (54,54), which puts its furthest point — the corner of a perforation
  tooth at (42,82) — 30.5 from the centre against the 33 allowed. A round mask,
  a squircle and a teardrop all leave it whole.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- Upper piece: rounded top, sheared off along the tear. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#F6F3EC"
        android:pathData="M43,26 h22 a5,5 0 0 1 5,5 V41 L38,55 V31 a5,5 0 0 1 5,-5 z" />

    <!-- Lower piece: the tear above, the perforated edge below. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#F6F3EC"
        android:pathData="M70,47 V78 l-4,4 l-4,-4 l-4,4 l-4,-4 l-4,4 l-4,-4 l-4,4 l-4,-4 V61 z" />
</vector>
